-- token economics --

-- before building an AI feature, it helps to estimate how many tokens it may use
-- tokens sent to the model are input tokens; tokens it replies with are output tokens
-- the program estimates the cost and checks usage against daily, monthly, RPM, and TPM limits
-- the .env file holds the values used for the estimate  

-- what i did  

I made a budget planner that estimates token use and cost. I also tested it; all four tests passed. When I doubled the daily requests, the estimated monthly cost doubled too.

Files: budget.py, test_budget.py, requirements.txt, .env
